WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:09.000
Welche jüdischen Feiertage sind für Dich besonders wichtig, wenn es um Exil, Freiheit und Gerechtigkeit geht?

00:10.766 --> 00:14.333
We have plenty of holidays that have

00:16.566 --> 00:20.266
Symbols of reminding us of

00:20.266 --> 00:22.100
the exile of Egypt.

00:23.100 --> 00:24.433
Because it was,

00:25.133 --> 00:26.733
It is considered to be

00:26.733 --> 00:31.866
one of the main things in Judaism,

00:31.933 --> 00:34.466
This is very interesting,

00:35.366 --> 00:38.166
because the exodus of Egypt

00:38.166 --> 00:40.466
shows you, how Jewish people

00:42.033 --> 00:43.800
treat

00:45.233 --> 00:47.200
Freedom.

00:47.366 --> 00:51.066
Why is it so difficult for me as a Jewish person,

00:51.233 --> 00:55.033
to see other people enslaved like that?

00:55.566 --> 00:58.700
If you think about it there were plagues in Egypt.

00:58.700 --> 01:00.100
How many plagues were there,

01:00.533 --> 01:02.900
you remember? It was 10 plagues.

01:03.700 --> 01:06.033
Yet it was after the 8th or the 9th,

01:06.033 --> 01:07.966
that Pharaoh told Moses

01:07.966 --> 01:09.100
"Get your people and"...

01:09.300 --> 01:11.133
"Take your people and get the hell out of here"

01:11.300 --> 01:13.133
But yet there was a 10th plague,

01:13.400 --> 01:15.066
the most horrific one.

01:15.100 --> 01:18.300
What was it for? Moses said to Pharaoh,

01:18.733 --> 01:21.900
"I will take till the last horses of your stables"

01:21.966 --> 01:25.366
"Everyone that is being enslaved by you will walk free"

01:25.366 --> 01:27.100
"when the Jewish people walk free"

01:29.166 --> 01:31.066
And, that is the Jewish standard.
